              ],
              "content": "Figure 4.8 (a) Two possible carbon-skeletons"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.197,
            0.624,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": "**Filling the remaining valencies with hydrogen gives us –**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.235,
            0.295,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.396,
            0.218,
            0.526,
            0.302
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.139,
                0.304,
                0.682,
                0.32
              ],
              "content": "Figure 4.8 (b) Complete molecules for two structures with formula $\\mathrm { C _ { 4 } H _ { 1 0 } }$"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.325,
            0.721,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": "**We see that both these structures have the same formula** $\\mathrm { C _ { 4 } H _ { 1 0 ^ { \\circ } } }$ **Such compounds with identical molecular formula but different structures are called structural isomers.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.372,
            0.722,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": "**In addition to straight and branched carbon chains, some compounds have carbon atoms arranged in the form of a ring. For example, cyclohexane has the formula** $\\mathrm { C _ { 6 } H _ { 1 2 } }$ **and the following structure –**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.454,
            0.241,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.177,
                0.521,
                0.199,
                0.534
              ],
              "content": "(a)"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.397,
            0.426,
